proofs:
EXISTING CONTAINERS UNCHANGED, R-4 shape (≥1 Hide): migration sets Other = Hide, which puts it in `hidden`. That changes nothing:
- no shown group (only shown categories emit groups);
- no exclusion in the catch-all (excludeGuarded no-op);
- supersedesCatchAll unchanged (O not shown);
- hasUnion unchanged (the union is built from spells-kind lists only);
- finishWarnings' anyHidden unchanged (already true);
- the noIds roles of every group unchanged.
This holds for each sub-shape: U Hide (the catch-all is suppressed either way); U Show on player/pet buffs (the U group's exclude-union is unchanged and draws unlisted Other auras, Uncategorized Show beating Other Hide under rule 3); U Show on target/focus buffs (the catch-all = Ocon ∧ unlisted still ships, now read as Uncategorized Show beating Other Hide where the union cannot be applied); and every HARMFUL R-4 (its catch-all is already dropped as a provenance conflict). Other = Show would NOT preserve R-4: it adds a group, rescues Other-auras on Hidden spell lists (Show beats Hide), supersedes the catch-all, and adds an Other group to the no-ids view.

tests:
test_migrations / test_database_categories, v12 unit cases, each against Database.MigrateV12 on raw tables:
(a) an all-Show container gets other = show and otherDebuffs = show;
(b) a buff container with one buff Hide gets other = hide, while otherDebuffs follows its HARMFUL states;
